Name Soils Kernels Concrete shells Two-terminal sources Junctions Voltage sources Status <code>image</code> homogeneous (forwards two- and multi-layer) line, point yes yes yes yes default <code>image_2layer</code> two-layer line, point yes yes yes yes <code>mom</code> homogeneous, two-layer point yes (since 2026.11) yes yes yes <code>mom_sommerfeld</code> any number of layers point yes (since 2026.11) yes yes yes options: <code>MomSommerfeldOptions</code> <code>fem</code> any number of layers — yes (since 2026.11) yes (since 2026.11) yes (since 2026.11) yes (since 2026.11) experimental; axisymmetric model for coaxial rods and rings, 3-D model otherwise (<code>fem3d</code> extra); options: <code>FemOptions</code> <code>cim</code> → <code>image</code> deprecated alias <code>bem</code> → <code>mom</code> deprecated alias <code>image_nlayer</code> homogeneous, two-layer line, point yes yes yes yes deprecated name of the <code>image</code> dispatch <p>Every built-in backend honours every conductor model (lumped, distributed, inductive, skin effect). Since its conforming model of 2026.11 (user decision Q37) <code>fem</code> runs the network of the shared pipeline like the integral backends: its axisymmetric model solves rods on one vertical axis and horizontal rings centred on it, its three-dimensional model (the optional <code>fem3d</code> extra) every other world, galvanic distributed conductors included (<code>FemOptions.model</code>). Up to then it solved distributed and inductive conductors as lumped resistive branches and rejected shells, junctions, two-terminal and voltage sources. The table is checked against the registry:</p> <pre><code>import groundfield as gf
from groundfield.solver import get_backend

assert gf.available_backends() == ("image", "image_2layer", "mom", "mom_sommerfeld", "fem")
assert set(gf.available_backends(include_deprecated=True)) - set(gf.available_backends()) == {
    "cim", "bem", "image_nlayer"
}

caps = {name: get_backend(name).capabilities for name in gf.available_backends()}
assert caps["image"].kernels == {"line", "point"} and caps["mom"].kernels == {"point"}
assert caps["mom_sommerfeld"].soils == {"homogeneous", "two_layer", "multi_layer"}
assert caps["image"].concrete_shells and caps["mom"].concrete_shells
assert caps["mom_sommerfeld"].concrete_shells and caps["fem"].concrete_shells
assert caps["fem"].two_terminal_sources and caps["fem"].junctions
assert caps["fem"].conductors == {"lumped", "distributed", "inductive", "skin"}
assert all(caps[n].voltage_sources for n in gf.available_backends())
assert get_backend("fem").experimental
assert get_backend("cim").deprecated_alias_of == "image"
assert get_backend("bem").deprecated_alias_of == "mom"
</code></pre>
